            <ArticleTitle>[Intracranial subdural hematoma following spinal anesthesia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1596-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of intracranial subdural hematoma following spinal anesthesia in a 28-year-old woman. Subdural hematoma is a very rare, but life-threatening complication. When a patient complains of persistent post spinal headache, one should consider the possibility of subdural hematoma and carry out a careful examination, including MRI or CT scan.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
